General requirements:
- Read the problem carefully and identify exactly what value or expression is requested.
- Use exact arithmetic whenever possible. Keep radicals and fractions in simplest form.
- Reduce fractions to lowest terms. Simplify radicals.
- For modular/remainder questions, return the residue exactly in the requested modulus or residue class format.
- For counting/probability/algebra/number theory problems, check all constraints, edge cases, and parity or divisibility conditions.
