- Linear in each variable (multilinear/trilinear) interpolation:
  - If f is linear in each of n variables and you know values on a 2^n grid (e.g., {a,b}^n), then f is uniquely determined as a multilinear polynomial with monomials being all products of distinct variables up to degree n (e.g., for n=3: 1, x, y, z, xy, xz, yz, xyz).
  - Solve the resulting linear system (exactly, using Fractions) to find coefficients, or use tensor-product Lagrange interpolation in each variable. Then evaluate f at the requested point.
