The problem asks for the number of "healthy paths" on a cube. A healthy path is defined as:
1.  Starts and ends at the same corner ($v_{start} = v_{end}$).
2.  Uses no edge more than once (an Eulerian trail or a closed trail).
3.  Uses at most two edges adjacent to any particular face.

Let $k$ be the number of edges in the path.
The cube has 6 faces. Each face has 4 edges.
The total sum of the number of edges in the path belonging to each face is equal to the sum of edges in the path multiplied by 2 (since every edge borders exactly two faces).
Let $c_f$ be the number of edges of the path on face $f$. We are given $0 \le c_f \le 2$ for all 6 faces.
Thus, the sum $\sum_{f} c_f \le 6 \times 2 = 12$.
Since $\sum_{f} c_f = 2k$, we have $2k \le 12$, so $k \le 6$.

